cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the thesis repository."
title: "Thesis Neuro: Transcript-Grounded SAE and fMRI Comparison Tools"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mora Soler"
    given-names: "Daniel Arturo"
abstract: >-
  Research software for testing whether transcript-grounded sparse-autoencoder
  features carry similar predictive structure in language models and in human
  fMRI responses during naturalistic story comprehension. The package extracts
  SAE features from Gemma 2 and Llama 3.1, aligns them to the fMRI repetition-time
  grid, fits matched ridge encoders to cortical parcels and to language-model
  targets, and compares the fitted structures through learned weights, feature
  importance, and representational similarity.
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - fMRI
  - sparse autoencoders
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - language models
  - encoding models
repository-code: "https://github.com/daMS2005/thesis_neuro"
url: "https://github.com/daMS2005/thesis_neuro"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-03
license: MIT
